                  {
                    "tab_title": "What is the bilona method?",
                    "tab_content": "Bilona is a traditional Vedic process: A2 milk is curdled, then hand-churned using a wooden mathani rotated with a hemp rope — no machine, no heat. The makkhan (butter) that rises is slow-cooked on a wood fire to get pure ghee.",
                    "_id": "1994cc8d"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "What makes A2 ghee different from regular ghee?",
                    "tab_content": "Regular commercial ghee can come from A1 milk (cross-bred cows). A2 ghee comes from indigenous desi cows. Combined with the bilona method, A2 bilona ghee retains more nutrients than machine-made ghee.",
                    "_id": "ed90cde3"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "Is this ghee A1 or A2?",
                    "tab_content": "[FILL IN: Confirm A2 from indigenous desi cows.]",
                    "_id": "60d113a4"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "What is the shelf life?",
                    "tab_content": "[FILL IN: 12–18 months from manufacture date stored in a cool, dry place. Add exact date from your lab report.]",
                    "_id": "399dbd85"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "How should I store it?",
                    "tab_content": "Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. Do not refrigerate — ghee is shelf-stable. Always use a dry spoon to prevent contamination.",
                    "_id": "7a320748"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "Does it become solid in winter?",
                    "tab_content": "Yes — completely natural and a sign of purity. Solid in cold weather, liquid in warm. Both are fine to consume.",
                    "_id": "42e82685"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "Can I return the product?",
                    "tab_content": "Returns accepted only for damaged or incorrect items within 48 hours of delivery. See our Return & Refund Policy.",
                    "_id": "2304e8e8"
                  },
                  {
                    "tab_title": "Do you ship pan-India?",
                    "tab_content": "Yes. Delivery takes 3–7 business days. See our Shipping Policy for zone-wise timelines.",
                    "_id": "3af36d63"
                  }
